{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"\nBoth $16x^2$ and $81$ are *perfect squares,* since $16x^2=(\\blueD{4x})^2$ and $81=(\\greenD{9})^2$.\n\n$16x^2-81 = (\\blueD{4x})^2-(\\greenD{9})^2$\n\nSo we can use the *difference of squares* pattern to factor.\n\n$\\blueD{a}^2 - \\greenD{b}^2 =(\\blueD{a}+\\greenD{b})(\\blueD{a}-\\greenD{b})$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In this case, $\\blueD{a}=\\blueD{4x}$ and $\\greenD{b}=\\greenD{9}$:\n\n$(\\blueD{4x})^2 - (\\greenD{9})^2 =(\\blueD{4x}+\\greenD{9})(\\blueD{4x}-\\greenD{9})$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$16x^2-81=(4x+9)(4x-9)$\n\n*Remember that you can always check your factorization by expanding it.*","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Factor completely.**\n\n$16x^2-81=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"buttonSets":["basic"],"buttonsVisible":"focused","considered":"correct","form":true,"functions":["f","g","h"],"key":0,"simplify":false,"times":false,"value":"(4x+9)(4x-9)"},{"buttonSets":["basic"],"buttonsVisible":"focused","considered":"correct","form":true,"functions":["f","g","h"],"key":1,"simplify":false,"times":false,"value":"-(9+4x)(9-4x)"}],"buttonSets":["basic"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
